// handed HAND_SKELETON and draws it. It lives in its own file, and is loaded only by
// game.js's Adventure view (dynamic import, like adventure-renderer.js), because it is
// ~50KB and School and Classic view never draw it.
//
// ⚠️ ART CREDIT: "Hand Skeleton", published by OpenClipart (the Openclipart account), found
// at https://freesvg.org/hand-skeleton (FreeSVG SVG ID 170541, dated 2019-04-12). LICENCE:
// PUBLIC DOMAIN — CC0 1.0 (https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/). No credit
// is required and none is owed; it is recorded so the next person knows where it came from
// and that it is safe to ship in a school app. The page names no individual artist.
// The drawing was optimised (svgo, integer coordinates: 327KB → 50KB, visually
// identical at any size we draw it) and each bone sorted into a finger — see below.
//
// ⚠️ HOW IT LIGHTS. Unlike the Classic hand (one outline, five clipped overlays) this is
// 145 separate bone shapes, so each shape simply says which finger it belongs to:
//   ray   'thumb' | 'index' | 'middle' | 'ring' | 'pinky' | 'palm' | 'line'
//   fill  its resting colour, hex without '#'
//   k     how much darker than the main bone colour it is (1 = main, ~0.9 = shadow)
// Lighting a finger paints its bones in the finger colour × k, so the shadow bones stay
// shadows. 'line' shapes (the hair-thin gray edge drawing) are never recoloured.
// ⚠️ THE SORTING IS BY POSITION, NOT BY NAME — the source file names nothing. 'palm' is
// the four metacarpals plus the wrist bones (what the big letter sits on); a finger is
// its phalanges only; the thumb includes its long metacarpal so it reads as one thumb.
// Redrawing or replacing the art means re-sorting; the groups were checked by painting
// each one a different colour and looking.
// ⚠️ A RIGHT hand, thumb on the left, like the Classic art; the left hand is its mirror.
